---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import HomeNavigation from "../components/HomeNavigation.astro";
import ThemeToggle from "../components/ThemeToggle.astro";
import Footer from "../components/Footer.astro";
import GhostRunner from "../components/GhostRunner.astro";
import ImageSlider from "../components/ImageSlider.astro";
import ImageToggle from "../components/ImageToggle.astro";
---

<Layout
	title="About | Narayan Ashanahalli"
	description="Product Designer & Prototyper building 0-to-1 experiences across AI, hardware, and digital infrastructure."
	fullWidth={true}
>
	<HomeNavigation />

	<div class="about-layout">
		<header class="about-header">
			<h1 class="about-title">About</h1>
		</header>

		<div class="about-divider"></div>

		<div class="about-content-grid">
			<div class="about-body">
				<p>
					👋 I'm Narayan Ashanahalli, a Product Designer &
					Prototyper building [0-to-1]&nbsp;experiences across AI,
					hardware, and digital infrastructure. With a foundation in
					architecture, I apply systems thinking and rapid
					prototyping to create digital products that feel responsive
					and grounded in existing ecosystems.
				</p>
				<p>
					🎯 I'm looking to work with people and teams shaping a new era of human–AI interaction—across physical AI, intelligent tools, and products that augment how people think, build, and live. People who are genuinely excited about this future and care as much about how these systems feel in use as what they can technically do.
				</p>
			</div>

			<div class="about-media">
				<ImageSlider
					variant="carousel"
					autoplay={true}
					indicatorType="dots"
					slides={[
						{
							src: "/assets/projects/about/1.jpeg",
							alt: "Narayan — photo 1",
							label: "01",
						},
						{
							src: "/assets/projects/about/2.jpeg",
							alt: "Narayan — photo 2",
							label: "02",
						},
						{
							src: "/assets/projects/about/3.jpg",
							alt: "Narayan — photo 3",
							label: "03",
						},
						{
							src: "/assets/projects/about/4-compressed.mp4",
							alt: "Narayan — video 4",
							label: "04",
						},
						{
							src: "/assets/projects/about/5-compressed.gif",
							alt: "Narayan — photo 5",
							label: "05",
						},
					]}
				/>
			</div>

			<div class="about-body">
				<p>
					❓The question I keep coming back to: how do we design AI that understands the context around what people are doing and becomes part of how they think and act, rather than another system they have to manage? And at the core how to build for the technology can work alongside people while the interaction stays grounded in the task, the environment, and what they are actually trying to do.
				</p>
				<p>
					🔧 I'm currently working as a Design Researcher at Lab 4
					Cybernetics with <a
						href="https://pangaro.com/"
						target="_blank"
						rel="noopener noreferrer">Paul Pangaro</a
					>, building the lab's digital infrastructure: <a
						href="https://lab4cybernetics.vercel.app"
						target="_blank"
						rel="noopener noreferrer">the website</a
					>, a practitioner-scholar <a
						href="https://l4cybernetics.vercel.app/matching"
						target="_blank"
						rel="noopener noreferrer">matching platform</a
					>, and a knowledge graph system organizing <a
						href="https://publish.obsidian.md/lab4c"
						target="_blank"
						rel="noopener noreferrer">cybernetics concepts</a
					>.
				</p>
				<p>
					🤖 My thesis project, supported by the <a
						href="https://studioforcreativeinquiry.org/frff-grants-microgrants"
						target="_blank"
						rel="noopener noreferrer">Frank-Ratchye Further Fund</a
					>, explores how physically embodied AI can provide spatial
					task assistance through laser-pointing, bridging LLM
					reasoning with physical spatial referencing.
				</p>
				<p>
					💡 I'm learning that the best way to understand a new interaction is by building it. I design through building—moving between research, interaction design, prototyping, and code, using each to sharpen the others without losing the original intent. AI makes this process even more powerful by letting us build and learn in the same loop, while developing the judgment and heuristics to know what to preserve, what to question, and what the interaction should become.
				</p>
			</div>
		</div>

		<Footer />
		<div class="game-bottom-wrapper">
			<GhostRunner />
		</div>
	</div>

	<div class="toggle-floater">
		<div class="sidebar-controls">
			<ThemeToggle />
		</div>
	</div>
</Layout>

<style>
	.about-layout {
		width: 100%;
		max-width: 100%;
		box-sizing: border-box;
		padding: 140px 48px 0;
		margin: 0;
		background: var(--bg-primary);
		min-height: 100vh;
	}

	.toggle-floater {
		position: fixed !important;
		bottom: 20px !important;
		right: 20px !important;
		top: auto !important;
		margin: 0 !important;
		padding: 0 !important;
		z-index: 9999 !important;
		width: auto;
		display: flex;
		justify-content: flex-end;
	}

	.sidebar-controls {
		display: flex;
		gap: 1rem;
		align-items: center;
	}

	.about-header {
		max-width: 860px;
		margin-bottom: 48px;
		text-align: left;
	}

	.about-title {
		font-family: "Google Sans", sans-serif;
		font-size: 48px;
		font-weight: 450;
		line-height: 1.05;
		color: var(--text-primary);
		margin: 0;
	}

	.about-divider {
		width: 100%;
		height: 1px;
		background: var(--border-subtle);
		margin-bottom: 48px;
	}

	.about-content-grid {
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
		gap: 0;
		align-items: center;
		margin-bottom: 96px;
	}

	.about-body {
		display: flex;
		flex-direction: column;
		gap: 1.5rem;
		max-width: 860px;
	}

	.about-image-break {
		width: 100%;
		display: flex;
		justify-content: center;
		align-items: flex-start;
		margin: 1.5rem 0;
	}

	.about-image-break :global(.image-toggle-component) {
		width: 100%;
		max-width: 100%;
		text-align: left;
	}

	.about-media {
		width: 100%;
		max-width: 860px;
	}

	/* This is the clipping boundary (overflow: hidden on .image-slider) -
	   widening it just gives the peeking prev/next slides more room to
	   show before getting cut off. It does NOT change how big the active
	   image looks; that's fixed separately below. Centered within the
	   860px text-body width above (.about-media matches .about-body's
	   max-width) rather than the full page width. */
	.about-media :global(.image-slider.constrained) {
		max-width: 600px;
		margin-left: auto;
		margin-right: auto;
	}

	/* No cropping, no fixed frame: each slide sizes itself to its own
	   image's natural aspect ratio instead of being forced into a
	   shared box (which would need a letterbox band to avoid cropping).
	   Different slides can be different heights here. Fixed px (not a %
	   of the clipping box above) so widening that box doesn't scale the
	   image up - it only adds peek margin. Scoped to this page only. */
	.about-media :global(.image-slider[data-variant="carousel"] .slider-display) {
		aspect-ratio: auto;
		height: auto;
		width: 380px;
		max-width: 100%;
	}

	.about-media :global(.image-slider[data-variant="carousel"] .slider-track) {
		height: auto;
		align-items: center;
	}

	.about-media :global(.image-slider[data-variant="carousel"] .slide) {
		height: auto;
	}

	/* Visually pull the peeking side slides closer to overlap the
	   active one, using transform (not margin) so the flex layout
	   itself is untouched and the active slide's centered position
	   (driven by the track's own translateX) can't be thrown off. */
	.about-media :global(.image-slider[data-variant="carousel"] .slide.prev) {
		transform: scale(0.85) translateX(40px);
	}

	.about-media :global(.image-slider[data-variant="carousel"] .slide.next) {
		transform: scale(0.85) translateX(-40px);
	}

	.about-media :global(.image-slider[data-variant="carousel"] .optimized-slide-image) {
		width: 100%;
		height: auto;
		object-fit: contain;
	}

	.about-media :global(.image-slider[data-variant="carousel"] .slide .optimized-slide-image) {
		border: 1px solid var(--border-subtle);
		border-radius: var(--radius-md);
	}

	.about-body p {
		font-family: var(--font-sans);
		font-size: 1.5rem;
		line-height: 1.4;
		color: var(--text-secondary);
		font-weight: 300;
		text-align: left;
		margin: 0;
	}

	.about-body a {
		color: inherit;
		text-decoration: underline;
		text-underline-offset: 3px;
		text-decoration-thickness: 1px;
	}

	.about-body a:hover {
		color: var(--accent-secondary);
	}

	:global(.about-layout) :global(.site-footer) {
		width: calc(100% + 96px) !important;
		margin-left: -48px !important;
		margin-right: -48px !important;
	}

	.game-bottom-wrapper {
		position: relative;
		width: calc(100% + 96px);
		margin-left: -48px;
		margin-top: 0px;
		margin-bottom: 0px;
		z-index: 0;
	}

	.game-bottom-wrapper :global(.ghost-game-container) {
		border-radius: 0;
		border: none;
		border-top: 1px solid var(--border-subtle);
		width: 100%;
	}

	@media (max-width: 1024px) {
		.about-title {
			font-size: 64px;
		}
		.about-content-grid {
			gap: 0;
		}
	}

	@media (max-width: 640px) {
		.about-layout {
			padding: 100px 16px 0;
		}
		:global(.about-layout) :global(.site-footer) {
			width: calc(100% + 32px) !important;
			margin-left: -16px !important;
			margin-right: -16px !important;
		}
		.game-bottom-wrapper {
			width: calc(100% + 32px);
			margin-left: -16px;
		}
		.about-title {
			font-size: 40px;
		}
		.about-body p {
			font-size: 1.1rem;
		}
	}
</style>

<script>
	document.addEventListener("astro:page-load", () => {
		// Floating Theme Toggle Footer Collision Logic
		const toggleFloater = document.querySelector(
			".toggle-floater",
		) as HTMLElement;
		const footer = document.querySelector(".site-footer") as HTMLElement;
		if (toggleFloater && footer) {
			const updateTogglePosition = () => {
				const footerRect = footer.getBoundingClientRect();
				const windowHeight = window.innerHeight;
				const margin = 20;

				if (footerRect.top < windowHeight) {
					const offset = windowHeight - footerRect.top + margin;
					toggleFloater.style.setProperty(
						"bottom",
						`${offset}px`,
						"important",
					);
				} else {
					toggleFloater.style.setProperty(
						"bottom",
						"20px",
						"important",
					);
				}
			};

			window.addEventListener("scroll", updateTogglePosition, {
				passive: true,
			});
			window.addEventListener("resize", updateTogglePosition);
			updateTogglePosition();
		}
	});
</script>
